Subject: [PATCH] T23: apply structural OSD changes (enable/disable + logo) live, no encoder teardown
Target: prudynt-t @ f4b32289359d176fb0795d9f3735af0bd9d6d2fd (branch stable)
Stacks on: 0001-0016 (no prior patch touches OSD.cpp/OSD.hpp).
Applies with git apply -p1 / patch -p1 AFTER 0001-0016.

==== Why ====
The Web UI sends action.restart_thread=ThreadOSD (bit 8) for OSD edits, but f4b3228
handle_action decodes only bits 1/2/4 (rtsp/video/audio), so item enable/disable and
logo on/off persist to config but are NOT applied until the next prudynt restart. The
reference firmware applied them live via global_restart_video (a full encoder/VPU
rebuild) -- which on T23 f4b3228 is the issue2 VPU freeze (see 0002/0003). We must apply
these changes at the OSD-region layer ONLY, never touching the encoder/framesource/VPU
or the OSD group binding.

==== What ====
1) OSD::init(): create the time/usertext/uptime/logo regions UNCONDITIONALLY (was: only
   if enabled) and set the group region 'show' flag = <item>_enabled ? 1 : 0. All in-scope
   regions therefore exist after init, disabled ones simply hidden. (brightness unchanged.)
2) New OSD::applyStructural(): toggles each created region's visibility with
   IMP_OSD_ShowRgn(rgn, osdGrp, enabled?1:0). No CreateRgn/DestroyRgn/DestroyGroup at
   runtime -> cannot hit the issue2 bound-node-destroy freeze.
3) video_stream gains std::atomic<bool> osd_reinit (mirrors 0004's req_*/reconfig idiom).
4) JsonAPI handle_action decodes bit 8 (ThreadOSD) -> sets osd_reinit=true on every
   video stream (NOT global_restart_video).
5) OSD::thread_entry consumes osd_reinit.exchange(false) on the OSD worker thread (the
   only thread that calls IMP_OSD_*) and runs applyStructural() -> live within ~100ms.

SCOPE / NOT covered (still need a streamer restart): font_size / stroke_size live (needs
libschrift re-init + glyph-cache clear), and turning a stream's WHOLE OSD on from fully
off (no OSD object/worker exists when stream.osd.enabled=false at encoder create).

NOTE: UNTESTED on-device at time of authoring. Must be built (prudynt-binary CI) and
verified on hardware (toggle each OSD item live + confirm the stream never freezes)
before relying on it. Rollback = delete this file (reverts to apply-on-restart, safe).

